  } catch (error) {
    expect((error as Error).message).toBe("already_enrolled");
  }
});

$ npx vitest run enrollments
 ✓ enrollments.test.ts > refuses a second enrollment in the same course

A pull request changes enroll so that the second call resolves normally and inserts a second row.

Statement: "After that pull request, this test still passes."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. When the second enroll resolves, the catch block never runs, so the only expect in the test never runs either. A test that finishes without a failed assertion passes, even with zero assertions. Rewrite it as await expect(enroll("u1", "sql-basics")).rejects.toThrow("already_enrolled"), or at least add expect.assertions(1) at the top, and the pull request turns it red. The misconception is that an expect written in the test always runs; inside catch, .then or a loop it only runs if the code goes that way.', 2, 5
