Statement: "Because the system time is frozen, day is 1 on the laptop and on the CI runner."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. vi.setSystemTime freezes an instant: 2026-11-01T06:30:00+07:00 is 2026-10-31T23:30:00Z everywhere. getDate() then converts that instant to the local time zone of the process running the test, so the laptop in UTC+7 gets 1 (1 November, 06:30) and the UTC runner gets 31 (31 October, 23:30). The misconception is that a fake clock makes all date arithmetic deterministic; it fixes the instant, not the time zone. Use getUTCDate() with an explicit offset, or Intl.DateTimeFormat with a timeZone option, and run the suite with TZ=UTC as well as your local zone.', 1, 5
