Statement: "The second test fails in the full run because the first test changed the shared config object and nothing restores it before the second test runs."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'True. config is created once when the module is imported, and both tests in the file use that same object. Tests in one file run one after another in the order they are written (Vitest''s default), so the second test sees maxAttempts 3 left behind by the first and 4 < 3 is false. Run alone with -t, the first test is skipped and maxAttempts is still 5, so it passes. The misconception is that a test which passes alone must be correct, or that the failure is random: it fails every time the first test runs before it. The fix is to stop changing shared state (pass the limit in, or build the config per test) or to restore it in beforeEach, not to reorder the tests.', 1, 5
