Statement: "Because Vitest gives each test file its own module graph by default (the isolate option), these two files cannot affect each other through the database."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Isolation per test file is about memory: each file gets fresh copies of the modules it imports, so a module-level cache does not leak from one file to another. Both files still connect to the same PostgreSQL database, and Vitest runs test files in parallel workers by default, so both can insert learner@codedev.test at about the same time, and the beforeAll in users.test.ts can delete the row the other file just created. The misconception is that the test runner''s isolation covers external resources. The fix is unique data per test (for example an e-mail with randomUUID()), a transaction rolled back per test, or one database per worker; running with --no-file-parallelism only hides the problem.', 2, 5
