Statement: "Merging PR #611 fixes the pipeline: a test that fails and then passes on a retry has shown that the code works."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. A retry runs the same test again until the dice come up right; it changes how often the build is red, not why. The leaderboard test is pointing at a real bug - production ranks tied learners by insertion order, not by name - and with three retries it would almost always go green and hide it. The enrolment test would keep failing about one run in seven and pass on the retry, so every future timing bug in that file would be hidden too. Retries can be acceptable for a short time on tests that cross a real network, with a ticket to remove them; for unit tests that depend on the clock and on order they only remove the signal. The misconception is that a green retry is evidence; it is a second sample of a random result.', 4, 5
