Statement: "After the fix, five passing CI runs in a row show that the flakiness is gone."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. Before the fix the pipeline already passed 4 runs in 5, so five green runs in a row happen with probability 0.8^5, about 33%, on code that is still broken - and the default file order may never put streak.test.ts before leaderboard.test.ts. Useful evidence forces the conditions that caused the failures: run the suite many times (for example 100) with a shuffled order and a different seed each time, and pin the clock to the edge of a second (07:09:40.999) in a test. A broken pipeline passes 100 runs with probability 0.8^100, about 2 in 10 billion. The misconception is that a few green runs prove the absence of a random failure.', 6, 5
