One mutant survives every test, even after a reviewer added more cases:
[Survived] EqualityOperator  src/checkout/coupon.ts:4
-  if (price <= MIN_PRICE) return price;
+  if (price < MIN_PRICE) return price;

Statement: "This mutant shows a missing test: a case with a price of exactly 10,000 VND will kill it."', 'single_choice'::question_type, 'False. The mutant only behaves differently when price is exactly 10,000. There the original returns 10,000 at once; the mutant goes on, computes some discount d and returns Math.max(10,000 - d, 10,000), which is 10,000 again. No input gives a different result, so no test can kill it: it is an equivalent mutant. The right response is to confirm that by reasoning (as here), then mark it as ignored with a comment in the code or exclude it in the tool''s configuration, not to keep adding tests. The misconception is that every survivor is a missing test; most are, but equivalent mutants are why a 100% mutation score is not a useful target.', 2, 5
    WHERE NOT EXISTS (SELECT 1 FROM challenge.questions WHERE challenge_id = (SELECT id FROM challenge.challenges WHERE public_id = 'chal_quiz_ttd_341') AND order_index = 2)
    RETURNING id
